### Teko build artifacts ###
# (0.3.0.30 taxonomy) `.tkb` is now EXCLUSIVELY the Teko Binary codec artifact (docs/design/
# tkr-regression-format.md §0) — always a build product, always ignored. The authored regression
# specs are `.tkr` (Gherkin, tracked by default, no rule needed).
*.tkb
*.tkcov

### WASM test harness build output ###
*.wasm
*.wat
*.mjs
### Teko project build outputs (regenerated by `teko build`; never committed) ###
examples/**/*.c
examples/regressions/match_pattern_bindings/match_pattern_bindings
examples/regressions/optionals/optionals
examples/regressions/noncapturing_lambda_lift/noncapturing_lambda_lift

# native-backend build artifacts (teko build .)
/teko.c
/teko
/bin/
# native-build output dirs anywhere (teko build . -> <proj>/bin)
bin/
# gen2/paranoid fixpoint scratch build dirs (never committed — they perturb byte-identity)
bin2/
binp/
# (0.3.0.30 R2) the regression runner builds each curated regressor with `-o bin` relative to the
# regressor dir — keep those working trees clean so they never perturb the fixpoint / byte-identity
# checks. (Redundant with the global `bin/` above; named for the crumb.)
examples/regressions/**/bin/
# self-host verification output dirs (the gen1/gen2/gen3 byte-identity gate)
/gen1/
/gen2/
/gen3/
# dot-prefixed variants of the same gate dirs (.gen2/.gen3 — PR #100 committed them by accident)
.gen*/
# the fixpoint gate's own scratch root — the SAME accident as `.gen*/` above, with a name that
# `.gen*/` does not cover. PR #95 committed .fixpoint/gen2{,.c} and gen3{,.c}: 28 MB of generated
# artefacts, two of them 10 MB C files headed "generated by teko — do not edit". Generated C is
# OUTPUT and is never tracked; the one tracked C from this machinery is `bootstrap/teko.c`, and
# only because it is a deliberately harvested seed. No green was ever faked by this — the gate
# wipes its scratch root before it builds (scripts/fixpoint_gate.sh, `rm -rf "$W"`).
.fixpoint/
cobertura.xml

# per-worktree downloaded teko compiler (scripts/fetch_teko.sh)
.teko/
# per-worktree PROVISIONED seed (scripts/ci_provision_teko.sh) + downloaded archives — NEVER commit a binary
.seed/
teko-*.tar.gz
teko-*.zip
gd-*/
/out/
# throwaway gen1 self-host build dir (teko build . -o gen1out)
/gen1out/
/.work/
/build/
/bin/

# native-build output dir (teko build -> <proj>/target for some layouts) — NEVER commit
target/

# Transients left by a producer run executed IN-TREE (an agent measuring locally, or a hand-run
# of scripts/produce_assets.sh). In CI they live in a throwaway runner and nobody sees them; on a
# developer's or an agent's checkout they land next to the source and get swept into a `git add
# -A`, which is exactly how one of them nearly rode into a memory-file commit.
.teko-seed-fallback-wt/
.ci-phase-clock
.seed/
gd-*/
asset-log-*.txt

# build artefacts of the local trampoline (cc(bootstrap/teko.c) -> the wagon-15 compiler)
.rung-c/

# scratch of the regression pool runner tests (regression_test.tkt: run_pool_*/pool_*)
.regr-pool-*/
